<p>Iranian officials say an air strike hit the Shajare Tayyebeh girls’ elementary school in Minab, southern Iran, killing at least 150 people, including many children; some reports put the death toll at more than 165 or more than 170. UN rights chief Volker Turk called for a swift, transparent investigation and said those responsible should be held to account, while the U.S. Department of Defense says it is investigating the incident. Several outlets say the evidence available so far, along with U.S. statements about ongoing strikes near the Strait of Hormuz, points to American forces as the most likely source of the strike—though neither the United States nor Israel has claimed responsibility. A New York Times analysis cited by multiple articles links the timing of strikes on naval targets near the Strait of Hormuz—where an IRGC base is located—to the moment the school was hit, and Reuters cited two unnamed U.S. officials saying investigators believe U.S. forces were likely responsible. After the attack, Iran’s Revolutionary Guards say they targeted a U.S. base in the United Arab Emirates in retaliation, highlighting the risk of wider regional escalation even as calls grow for clearer facts and stronger safeguards to protect civilians.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oJgA5gLkgpK6Dpox4KJYEyiVdjoJRZ-TlzfeE7OHKBZzOwZS3-isZs-xlHv36DV7RGSF-sfRLZw_IWQzZN3lrnTnrYg5RGVR9Y7JBRaD' alt='A satellite image shows the Shajareh Tayyebeh girls’ school and other structures damaged after being struck in Minab, Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Context of the strike: Iranian officials said the Shajare Tayyebeh elementary school in Minab was hit on the first day of the war, in an area near sites controlled by the IRGC.</li><li>Attribution signals cited in reports: A New York Times analysis pointed to U.S. military statements about attacks on naval targets near the Strait of Hormuz (where an IRGC base is located) and matched the timing to when the school was hit; Reuters also cited two unnamed U.S. officials saying investigators believe U.S. forces were likely responsible.</li><li>UN language on accountability: Volker Turk said he expected investigations to be prompt and fully transparent, adding that “mistakes were clearly made,” and called for accountability.</li><li>Claims, investigation, and response: Neither the U.S. nor Israel has claimed responsibility; the Pentagon said it is investigating, while Iran’s Revolutionary Guards said they struck a U.S. base in the UAE in retaliation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Nations human rights office: In Geneva, rights chief Volker Turk told reporters the investigation should be prompt and fully transparent. He added that “mistakes were clearly made” and said accountability should follow. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979315/un-demands-swift-probe-into-us-strike-on-iran-girls-school'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>U.S. Department of Defense: The Pentagon says it is investigating the incident amid reports that U.S. forces may have been involved. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-girls-school-alleged-strike/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Iran’s Revolutionary Guards: The IRGC said it targeted a U.S. base in the UAE and described the strike as retaliation for the Minab school incident. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-guards-say-targeted-us-base-in-uae-over-school-strike-in-minab/article70713695.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Media investigations: Reporting cited a New York Times analysis that drew on U.S. military statements about strikes on naval targets near the Strait of Hormuz, alongside other media work comparing timing using social media and witness media from the area. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979315/un-demands-swift-probe-into-us-strike-on-iran-girls-school'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-evidence-iran-war-tehran-strike-school-us/'>Evidence suggests explosion at Iranian elementary school was likely from U.S. air strikes</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-guards-say-targeted-us-base-in-uae-over-school-strike-in-minab/article70713695.ece'>Iran Guards say targeted U.S. base in UAE over school strike in Minab</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979315/un-demands-swift-probe-into-us-strike-on-iran-girls-school'>UN demands swift probe into ‘US strike’ on Iran girls school</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-girls-school-alleged-strike/'>Iran says a girls&#x27; school was hit by a deadly air strike. Here&#x27;s what we know.</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-guards-say-targeted-us-base-in-uae-over-school-strike'>Iran’s Revolutionary Guards say targeted US base in UAE over school strike</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>